<title>GERMANY: German reform to cut 82 bln DM in tax - document.</title>
<headline>German reform to cut 82 bln DM in tax - document.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The tax reform draft hammered out by Germany's coalition on Wednesday will slash 81.9 billion marks in taxes but raise an extra 38.1 billion by broadening the tax base, a coalition paper showed on Thursday.</p>
<p>The net lightening of the tax load will come out at 43.8 billion marks as a result of measures intended to take effect in 1998 and 1999 -- the largest of which will be income tax reductions.</p>
</text>
